    <!-- Abstract -->
    <h2 id="Abstract">Abstract</h2>

    <pre>
This conference paper considers the cost and lifespan of bridge deck repairs.
Different repair options can be compared by considering their costs and
expected lifespans. The data presented can help demonstrate the relationship
between repair expenditure and durability.
    </pre>

    <hr>

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <h2 id="Introduction">Introduction</h2>

    <pre>
Bridge deck repairs are an important part of maintaining the safety and
durability of bridges. Selecting an appropriate repair method requires
consideration of both the initial cost and the expected lifespan of the repair.

This paper presents data relating to the cost and lifespan of different
repair options. The data is displayed in a table to support comparison
and discussion.
    </pre>

    <hr>

    <!-- Analysis and discussion -->
    <h2 id="Analysis-and-discussion">Analysis and Discussion</h2>

    <p>
        The table below compares the cost of repairs with the lifespan
        of each repair option. It provides a basis for discussing how
        repair costs vary with expected durability.
    </p>

    <!-- Repair data table -->
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>£ Cost of repairs</th>
            <th>Lifespan of repairs (years)</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>£0.7 million</td>
            <td>2</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>£3.3 million</td>
            <td>4</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
